    "contract": 1,
    "title": "Minimal GoGoGadget",
    "description": "The smallest closure that boots, not a small application: 167 modules. It names no component or element: every page, workflow and seam declares the UI it actually renders, derived with go/types from product code, so the closure installs the 66 ui modules its own pages reach instead of the 77 a hand-kept member list arrived at. The remaining floor is four seams naming product symbols in their own payloads. ggg/system/server owns internal/web/server.go, whose statically-declared capability fields name thirteen capabilities, and its auth.go and htmx.go call applyStoredAppearance, applyImpersonation and resolveTheme, which ggg/workflow/{appearance,impersonation} own. ggg/system/jobs's definitions.go names deliverWebhook, exportProjectsCSV and exportOrgJSON, owned by ggg/workflow/{outbound-webhooks,project-export,organization-export}. ggg/system/api's projects.go compiles against ggg/workflow/projects' sqlc queries. And migration 0020_provider_neutral_ids asserts a fixed fifteen-table shape before it renames anything, so no closure may omit the nine modules that create those tables. Each of those pulls pages, and a navigation entry's after must name an entry its area contains, so the settings and admin sidebars are chains a profile enters whole.",
